<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Korla</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Korla is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the north-eastern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a> at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian-shan">Tian Shan</a>, and the seat of the Bayingolin Mongol Autonomous Prefecture. An ancient oasis on the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>, it is where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaqub-beg">Yaqub Beg</a>, ruler of Yettishar, died in 1877 as Qing armies advanced. It has grown into a centre of the Tarim oil industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/korla.jpg" alt="Korla" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: liuzusai刘祖赛 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%AD%94%E9%9B%80%E6%B2%B3%E6%9A%AE%E8%89%B2_2016_%E5%88%98%E7%A5%96%E8%B5%9B_-_panoramio_(20).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
